[1mWhat the C actually does.[22m [38;5;10mstatic_alias[0m holds a function-local [38;5;10mstatic int inner = 1[0m and returns either [38;5;10m&inner[0m or the pointer it was given. Once it returns [38;5;10m&inner[0m, every later call receives [38;5;10mouter == &inner[0m, so [38;5;10m*outer >= inner[0m compares the variable against itself, is always true, and [38;5;10minner += *outer[0m becomes [38;5;10minner += inner[0m. The program is therefore a one-way state machine: it walks [38;5;10minitial_value[0m up by 1 per iteration while [38;5;10minitial_value < 1[0m, then flips to the aliased state and doubles forever, wrapping on [38;5;10mint[0m overflow. The Rust models the pointer as a [38;5;10mRef::Outer[0m/[38;5;10mRef::Inner[0m tag over two locals, which is observationally identical.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mOne real mismatch found, in the exit status.[22m On a closed stdout pipe ([38;5;10mdriver 5 5000000 | head -1[0m) the C program dies from [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m — shell status 141 — while the Rust program exited 0. Cause: the Rust runtime sets [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m to [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m, so writes to a broken pipe return [38;5;10mEPIPE[0m, and the translation discarded write errors with [38;5;10mlet _ = …[0m. Fixed by restoring the default disposition via [38;5;10msignal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL)[0m at the top of [38;5;10mmain[0m (declared [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m, no new dependency), and by wrapping stdout in a [38;5;10mBufWriter[0m so the write pattern matches C stdio's fully-buffered non-tty stdout rather than Rust's per-line [38;5;10mLineWriter[0m. Note this was invisible to any stdout-only comparison — the bytes that did get read were identical.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Everything else already matched and is now pinned by tests: errors going to stdout rather than stderr (the C uses [38;5;10mprintf[0m), the [38;5;10margc[0m-then-[38;5;10margv[1][0m-then-[38;5;10margv[2][0m check order, [38;5;10mstrtol[0m's "one digit is enough" acceptance ([38;5;10m12abc[0m → 12, [38;5;10m0x10[0m → 0), [38;5;10mlong[0m→[38;5;10mint[0m narrowing on both operands ([38;5;10m4294967300[0m yields exactly 4 lines), [38;5;10mLONG_MAX[0m/[38;5;10mLONG_MIN[0m saturation before narrowing, and two's-complement wrapping on overflow.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mVerification.[22m [38;5;10mtranslation/tests/differential.rs[0m has 20 tests, no [38;5;10m#[ignore][0m, spawning both binaries and comparing stdout, stderr and exit status including death-by-signal; the C reference is built via cmake on demand, so [38;5;10mcargo test[0m works from a clean tree. Coverage maps to every branch in [38;5;10mmain[0m and [38;5;10mstatic_alias[0m (table in [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m). Before writing the suite I ran ~5,000 randomized argv and arithmetic cases against both binaries. To confirm the suite is not vacuous I injected seven faults one at a time — wrong exit code, reworded message, the SIGPIPE fix removed, [38;5;10msaturating_add[0m, a broken [38;5;10mstrtol[0m clamp, errors to stderr, and [38;5;10minner += 1[0m instead of [38;5;10minner += inner[0m — and each was caught (1 to 11 failures). [38;5;10mc_src/[0m sources are unmodified; only the documented [38;5;10mbuild/[0m directory was created there.[0m[0m
